Reads the drive rows in the ledger. Each drive that launches takes the next id in
its project, D1, D2 and so on, with the label --label gave it, and every row it
appends carries that id. A drive with no end row is running when this checkout's
lease names it, and interrupted otherwise: it was killed before it could write
one.

--all reads every project in the per-user registry instead, and needs no
project, so it answers from anywhere. A project whose config or ledger will not
read says why and the rest still answer.

[1mSafety:[0m read-only. Reads ledger.jsonl and this checkout's lease. --all reads
every project in the per-user registry instead, each project's config, ledger
and lease, and needs no project.

[1mUsage:[0m
  drover drives [flags]

[1mExamples:[0m
  [35mdrover drives[0m                     [2m# this project's drives, newest first[0m
  [35mdrover drives --all[0m               [2m# every registered project's[0m
  [35mdrover drives --json[0m              [2m# an array, one object per drive:[0m
    [{"id":"D2","label":"night run","started":"2026-10-17T01:00:00-07:00",
      "queued":["4","5"],"jobs":2,"items":[{"id":"4","outcome":""},
        {"id":"5","outcome":"skipped","reason":"blocked by 4, which parked protected_paths for the operator"}],
      "running":true,"paused":true},
     {"id":"D1","started":"2026-10-16T22:00:00-07:00","queued":["1","2"],
      "ended":"2026-10-16T23:10:00-07:00","exit":0,
      "items":[{"id":"1","outcome":"ready_to_merge"},{"id":"2","outcome":"parked"}]}]
  [35mdrover drives --all --json[0m        [2m# an array, one object per project:[0m
    [{"project":"webapp","root":"/home/me/src/webapp","drives":[...]}]

  ended and exit are absent until the drive wrote its end row. items is each
  item's outcome from that row, and the ids queued at launch with an empty
  outcome until then, save one the drive already skipped, which its lease
  publishes as skipped with a reason. running is true while this checkout's lease names the
  drive, and paused while that lease reads paused (drive --pause).

[1mFlags:[0m
      --all    every project in the per-user registry, not just this one
  -h, --help   help for drives
      --json   emit the drives as JSON

[1mGlobal Flags:[0m
      --color mode     color terminal output: auto, always or never; --json, --events and files are never colored (default auto)
  -I, --ignore-stale   run even though .drover.toml or the generated agent instructions are older than this binary
      --no-color       the same as --color=never
